{t: 2001}
{st: Deodato / Phish}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 114}

{sot: Fanfare}
| C           | C           | C           | C           |
| Ab          | Bb          | C           | C           |
{eot}

{sot: Groove}
| Cm7         | Cm7   Cm6   | Cm7         | Cm7   Cm6   |
| Cm7         | Cm7   Cm6   | Cm7         | Cm7   Cm6   |
{eot}

{sot: Solo}
| Cm7         | Cm7         | Cm7         | Cm7         |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
Eumir Deodato Arrangement: Based on Strauss's fanfare, transformed into a
classic C minor jazz-funk groove popularized further in jam band settings.

Fanfare Opening: Play the iconic three-note rising motif (C - G - C) over a
sustained C major chord before dropping into the dramatic Ab to Bb resolving
step back to C.

Groove Section: The underlying vamp relies on a C Dorian field. Alternate
between Cm7 and Cm6 (or Cm9) to keep the rhythm guitar line syncopated and
moving.

Soloing: Stick primarily to C Dorian and C Minor Pentatonic scale choices over
the main funk vamp. Keep strumming tight and focused on the top four strings.
{eov}